</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; width: 100%; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr style="vertical-align: top; text-align: justify">
<td style="width: 0.25in"/><td style="width: 0.25in; text-align: left"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">b.</span></td><td style="text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">These
                                            crushed materials are then fed into an eddy current separator (or &#8220;magnetic sorter&#8221;),
                                            where the iron scrapes are separated and can be sold to customers. Copper, aluminum, steel,
                                            and zinc remain in the mixed metals (second iteration).</span></td>
